{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":50714,"duration_api_ms":49815,"num_turns":12,"result":"I rewrote the existing `CLAUDE.md` rather than starting a new one. I haven't built or run any lesson, and I didn't confirm that `generate_toc.py` and `rename.py` do what I describe.\n\n- **Build styles:** The old version said all lessons use libbpf and `make`. Lessons 1–10 and a few others have only a `.bpf.c`, and CI builds them with `ecc` and `ecli`. The new file covers both, plus the Rust, Go and CUDA exceptions.\n- **Setup:** `src/third_party/bpftool` and `blazesym` are git submodules. They are empty on a fresh clone, so the file now lists the `git submodule update` step and the CI build dependencies. It also notes that `libbpf` is a symlink into `bpftool`.\n- **Master build:** `make -C src` builds every lesson and `make -C src clean` cleans them.\n- **Testing:** There is no unit-test suite. CI builds a lesson, then runs it for 3 seconds with `sudo timeout -s 2 3`. An exit code of 124 counts as success, and CI only covers some lessons.\n- **Docs:** Each lesson has English and Chinese READMEs that should be kept in sync. `src/scripts/` holds the writing guidelines and a script that regenerates the table of contents.\n- **Removed:** The old directory-range groupings (for example \"`src/22-28,34`: Security\") and the lines about vmlinux headers and supported frameworks. I couldn't confirm the groupings, and the rest is easy to see in the repo.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"db139bf2-7be6-4e94-b0e6-24ccf1cf215a","total_cost_usd":0.2401383,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13938,"cache_read_input_tokens":351546,"output_tokens":5489,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13938},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":520,"cache_read_input